#. module: sale_order_type_automation_payment_pro
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_sale_order_type_automation_payment_pro
msgid ""
"===========================================\n"
"Sale Order Type Automation - Payment Pro\n"
"===========================================\n"
"\n"
"Bridge module between ``sale_order_type_automation`` and ``account_payment_pro``:\n"
"makes the sale order type automatic payment reconcile against the invoice created\n"
"by the flow instead of the partner's prior debt.\n"
"\n"
"Features\n"
"========\n"
"\n"
"- When a ``sale.order.type`` automates invoice creation and its payment\n"
"  (``payment_atomation = validate_payment``) on a company with ``account_payment_pro``\n"
"  enabled (``use_payment_pro = True``), the automatic payment is scoped to the invoice\n"
"  generated by the automation.\n"
"- Prevents ``account_payment_pro`` from loading the partner's whole open debt and\n"
"  reconciling an older invoice instead of the one created by the flow.\n"
"- Installs automatically (``auto_install``) only when both base modules coexist; both\n"
"  are left untouched.\n"
"\n"
"Technical Details\n"
"=================\n"
"\n"
"- New models: none.\n"
"- Inherited models: ``account.move``.\n"
"- Override of ``_prepare_dict_account_payment``: adds ``to_pay_move_line_ids`` to the\n"
"  payment values, set to the invoice open lines (``invoice.open_move_line_ids``).\n"
"  Passing the field explicitly in ``create`` makes the ORM skip\n"
"  ``account.payment._compute_to_pay_move_lines`` for that record (same mechanism as\n"
"  ``account.move.pay_now()``), so ``_add_all()`` does not replace the lines with the\n"
"  partner's full debt.\n"
"- Views: none.\n"
"- Data / security: none.\n"
"- Tests: ``tests/test_automation_payment_scope.py`` checks that, with a prior open\n"
"  invoice of the same partner, the automatic payment reconciles only the invoice of\n"
"  the flow and leaves the prior one unpaid.\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"1. Install ``sale_order_type_automation`` and ``account_payment_pro``; this module\n"
"   installs on its own when both are present.\n"
"2. Enable ``account_payment_pro`` on the company (``use_payment_pro``).\n"
"3. Configure a sale order type (``sale.order.type``) with\n"
"   ``payment_atomation = validate_payment`` and its payment journal.\n"
"4. Confirm a sale of that type: the automation creates and validates the invoice,\n"
"   registers the payment and reconciles it against that invoice, leaving any prior\n"
"   partner debt untouched.\n"
"\n"
"Architecture\n"
"============\n"
"\n"
"The module contributes a single override on ``account.move`` in\n"
"``models/account_move.py``. It extends, via ``super()``, the\n"
"``_prepare_dict_account_payment`` method defined by ``sale_order_type_automation``,\n"
"injecting the to-pay line scope that ``account_payment_pro`` reads. It defines no\n"
"models, views or data of its own: all the automation and payment business logic stays\n"
"in the base modules.\n"
"\n"
"Dependencies\n"
"============\n"
"\n"
"- ``sale_order_type_automation``\n"
"- ``account_payment_pro``\n"
"\n"
"Author\n"
